<h2>Where the deadlines actually come from</h2>
<p>The BNSS creates the appellate forums — the Sessions Court for convictions by Magistrates, the High Court for sessions trials, and so on — but the time limits live in the Schedule to the Limitation Act, 1963. Two articles do most of the work: Article 115 for appeals by the convicted person, and Article 114 for appeals against acquittal. Around them operate Section 12 (exclusion of time for certified copies), Section 5 (condonation), and the special-leave machinery of Section 419 BNSS for complainants seeking to challenge an acquittal.</p>

<table class="law">
  <tr><th>Appeal</th><th>Provision</th><th>Period</th><th>Starting point</th></tr>
